restart claude after any changes to skills

Claude loads only skill names and descriptions at startup, then matches incoming requests against those descriptions using semantic matching
You get a confirmation prompt before Claude loads the full skill content into context


skills.md vs claude.md

claude.md is a part of every conversation            --> use for project wide standards
skills.md loads when needed based on description     --> for task specific expertise


skills.md vs subagent
subagent is to delegate task and has a separate context
subagent don't automatically skills
built in agents (like explore, plan and verify) cant access skills at all. Only custom subagents can access skills and only when you list them
when you create a subagent you need to define a field skills and list the skills there


skills.md vs hooks
hooks for automated operation before and after claude performes an action

skills.md vs mcp 
mcp provides external tools


